WEBVTT

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:33.830
Mister...

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:44.080
Anybody!

00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:51.790
Th-The locomotive's gone.

00:01:51.790 --> 00:01:54.500
What the hell could have happened?

00:01:59.050 --> 00:02:02.550
Ah!  Ah-ah-ah!  It's you!

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:18.260
Akine-san, please
give us the details!

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:20.230
Oh, wow.  Thank you, thank you.

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:21.220
How are you
feeling, Chizuko-san?

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:24.580
Twenty Faces is dead, isn't he?

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:26.080
Chizuko-san, how was it?

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:28.460
What kind of things did Twenty Faces' gang do to you?

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:31.210
Come on now, guys.

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:35.770
You can get all the details some other day.  I'll put on a press conference.

00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:41.740
Her whereabouts unknown for over two years since being abducted by Twenty Faces, Mikamo Chizuko-san was...

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:47.390
...rescued by Mr. Akine, whose investigation had tracked her to England.  She returned to Japan safely today.

00:02:57.180 --> 00:03:00.610
Madam, the young lady has returned.

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:05.780
Is that so?  And luckily I've just finished cooking.

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:12.140
She hasn't spoken a word or eaten a meal since then.

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:13.580
What a creepy girl.

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:20.020
Oh, my, my–

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:21.460
Chizuko-san!

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:24.880
You're back safely!  It's like a dream!

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:32.960
Ahem...

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:38.400
Thank you so very much for making this possible, Detective Akine.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:41.080
No, no.  Just doing my job.

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:46.060
But, you know, I do wonder what happened when she was held by Twenty Faces' gang!

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:49.410
But, you know, I can imagine what it was like.

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:51.730
They must have beat the crap out of her and–

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:54.290
Akine-san, let's talk about that another day.

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:57.190
Oh, right.  I see.  Where are my manners?

00:03:57.190 --> 00:04:01.450
Nevertheless, what about all the reporters lying in wait out front?

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:06.780
Ah, regarding that.  I shall leave it to you to handle all the interactions with them from here on.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:09.230
Oh, of course.

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:11.310
Leave it all to me!

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:12.950
Kurosaki.

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:15.020
Yes?

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:17.380
This is my lawyer.

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:20.880
Kurosaki here will explain everything in detail.

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:21.530
OK.

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:27.420
I will contact you in a couple of days about scheduling an appointment.

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:30.040
OK.  I will be waiting patiently.

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:34.640
Geez, Mrs. Mikamo puts on quite an act.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:37.890
She shouldn't be so apathetic about Chizuko-kun's return.

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:40.090
She even shed some crocodile tears earlier.

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:47.170
Well, she's the sort of woman to invite that young lawyer into her home the moment her husband died.

00:04:47.170 --> 00:04:51.100
Well, I supposed she wanted a young man in the house to fool around with.

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:59.130
I've been so worried about your safety all this time.

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:03.320
And right up until the end, all he talked about was you.

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:10.100
Tome, please leave the two of us alone.

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:12.170
Very good, madam.

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:31.570
It's incredible that you're all right.

00:05:31.570 --> 00:05:33.520
The train exploded, didn't it?

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:41.540
That's what he gets.  That man, Twenty Faces, is dead now, isn't he?

00:05:53.230 --> 00:05:57.210
Here, I made this soup for you.

00:05:57.210 --> 00:05:58.960
Eat up.

00:05:59.870 --> 00:06:01.420
Come now.

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:03.940
Before it cools down.

00:06:03.940 --> 00:06:04.920
Come on.

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:19.440
That's a good girl.

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:22.280
Eat as much as you can.

00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:33.830
Young lady...

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:43.790
Uhm...

00:06:51.650 --> 00:06:53.720
My name is Tome.

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:58.870
I'll do everything I can to ensure that you get better.

00:07:27.870 --> 00:07:32.080
You should get some rest, young lady.

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:34.150
I don't want to fall asleep.

00:07:34.150 --> 00:07:35.530
If I do, I'll dream.

00:07:45.280 --> 00:07:47.040
I feel so bad for her.

00:07:47.930 --> 00:07:52.410
She must have experienced such horrors from Twenty Faces' gang.

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:56.820
I have to do my best to support her.

00:08:00.350 --> 00:08:02.790
You guys again?

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:06.950
Chizuko-kun's mind and body are both still very weak.

00:08:06.950 --> 00:08:09.280
I'll be happy to field any questions you may have.

00:08:09.850 --> 00:08:12.820
Geez, let us see Chizuko-san already!

00:08:12.820 --> 00:08:13.720
Yeah, let us see her!

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:17.370
She must have seen some real atrocities, huh?

00:08:17.370 --> 00:08:19.590
Being with such a violent scoundrel.

00:08:19.590 --> 00:08:21.220
What did I tell you?

00:08:21.220 --> 00:08:26.230
As I said, I'll be the one to provide you with detailed information, even regarding those circumstances.

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:28.730
Whatever, let us see her already please!

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:31.230
It's not a scoop if we just talk to you.

00:08:35.250 --> 00:08:37.410
Come now, young lady.

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:40.030
Let's have breakfast out in the garden.

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:44.960
You'll wilt if you don't get some sunlight once in a while.

00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:50.360
Come now, right this way.

00:08:53.700 --> 00:08:56.200
I'll go and bring your breakfast now.

00:09:03.590 --> 00:09:05.600
Good morning, Chizuko-san.

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:09.560
Please don't worry.

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:11.270
I'm not someone you need to worry about.

00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:15.650
I'm a detective, you see.

00:09:15.650 --> 00:09:17.410
I'm searching for Twenty Faces.

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:20.810
You're searching for him?

00:09:21.320 --> 00:09:22.290
Yes.

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:27.880
You certainly don't seem to harbor any ill will towards him.

00:09:29.650 --> 00:09:36.820
There's a lot of amusing gossip out there about the bad deeds you were exposed to by Twenty Faces' gang.

00:09:37.370 --> 00:09:39.290
But I feel differently myself.

00:09:39.290 --> 00:09:44.590
Twenty Faces is not just some foolish man trying to get written up in the gossip columns.

00:09:45.550 --> 00:09:52.190
However, the montage you painted of him for the police was of a pretty bad person.

00:09:53.270 --> 00:09:55.650
Do you know much about him?

00:09:55.650 --> 00:09:57.650
I certainly do.

00:09:57.650 --> 00:10:01.700
That being said, I've yet to see his true face.

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:03.430
"Yet"?

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:05.660
But he's already...

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:09.460
Do you believe that Twenty Faces is really dead?

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:18.340
That's what I came to ask you.

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:21.110
I'll come back again.

00:10:21.850 --> 00:10:25.340
There's plenty more I'd like to ask you about.

00:10:25.340 --> 00:10:27.980
Well then, that's all for today.

00:10:29.180 --> 00:10:30.320
Mr. Detective...

00:10:31.720 --> 00:10:33.380
May I ask for your name?

00:10:34.030 --> 00:10:35.880
I'm called Akechi.

00:10:36.480 --> 00:10:37.880
Akechi-san...

00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:41.820
I'll look forward to our next meeting.

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:54.520
Young lady, was someone here?

00:10:55.020 --> 00:10:58.010
Oh?  You must be imagining things, Tome-san.

00:10:59.460 --> 00:11:03.530
You remembered my name, young lady!

00:11:12.050 --> 00:11:14.540
Now go ahead and eat up.

00:11:15.050 --> 00:11:19.260
The madam got up early to prepare you soup again this morning.

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:21.530
What about these rice balls?

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:23.890
I made them.

00:11:23.890 --> 00:11:27.660
Because I know you never eat your bread.

00:11:29.060 --> 00:11:30.400
I'll eat now.

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:38.050
It's delicious.

00:11:38.050 --> 00:11:40.290
I'm so glad.

00:11:40.290 --> 00:11:42.430
OK, now eat the soup before it gets cold.

00:11:45.570 --> 00:11:47.900
I don't need the soup.

00:11:56.010 --> 00:12:01.690
But I'm talking about the girl who was carried off by that Twenty Faces character.

00:12:01.690 --> 00:12:04.240
She's worth her weight in gold.

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:05.640
Her weight in gold?

00:12:05.640 --> 00:12:11.100
Yup.  I heard she knows where Twenty Faces' gang hid their spoils.

00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:13.210
Wow, that's something else.

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:16.580
So whoever can catch her and get her to spill the beans will be rich.

00:12:18.470 --> 00:12:25.020
But, heh, who knows what kind of things they made that girl go through.

00:12:25.020 --> 00:12:27.440
Twenty Faces' spoils?

00:12:28.660 --> 00:12:30.310
What's the matter?

00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:36.630
It'll get cold, Chizuko-san.

00:12:39.350 --> 00:12:42.260
Aunt, I'm going to go to school.

00:12:43.350 --> 00:12:45.110
School?  You?

00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:48.620
If I don't make an effort to go outside, I'll wilt.

00:12:52.020 --> 00:12:52.930
What is it?

00:12:53.770 --> 00:12:58.440
My apologies.  Her choice of words was funny.

00:12:59.320 --> 00:13:00.070
Thanks for the food.

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:02.660
H-Hey, Chizuko-san...

00:13:02.660 --> 00:13:06.050
I'll bring dinner to your room later.

00:13:10.210 --> 00:13:14.080
Watch, listen, and think for myself.

00:13:14.780 --> 00:13:16.950
That's it, right, Mister?

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:36.380
This should be interesting.

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:46.200
There!

00:13:46.200 --> 00:13:48.710
Over here!

00:13:48.710 --> 00:13:49.760
Heads up!

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:53.160
Did you hear?  Apparently she's never gone to school before.

00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:55.940
And she was abducted by a bad guy.

00:13:55.940 --> 00:13:57.520
Poor thing.

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:09.470
Humpty Dumpty sat on a wall.

00:14:09.470 --> 00:14:12.070
Humpty Dumpty had a great fall.

00:14:12.070 --> 00:14:13.660
All the king's horses and–

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:16.120
Words are very important.

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:18.160
Especially for people like us.

00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:20.900
They allow us to avoid unnecessary disputes.

00:14:20.900 --> 00:14:22.440
You understand, don't you?

00:14:22.440 --> 00:14:23.170
Yes.

00:14:23.170 --> 00:14:26.680
OK, Miss Mikamo, continue reading.

00:14:26.680 --> 00:14:28.290
Miss Mikamo.

00:14:28.290 --> 00:14:29.200
Yes, ma'am.

00:14:29.670 --> 00:14:31.490
Read aloud from page 17.

00:14:31.490 --> 00:14:32.060
Yes, ma'am.

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:36.810
Jack and Jill went up the hill to fetch a pail of water.

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:40.880
Jack fell down and broke his crown and Jill came tumbling after.

00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:44.520
That was excellent.  You must have had a great teacher.

00:14:45.450 --> 00:14:46.990
Thank you.

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:50.820
Up Jack got and home did trot as far as he could cap–

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:56.610
H-Hey, Mikamo-san.

00:14:58.770 --> 00:15:01.660
If you're OK with it, will you hang out with us this afternoon?

00:15:01.660 --> 00:15:02.500
Sure.

00:15:05.830 --> 00:15:10.780
Let us know if you need help with anything, Mikamo-san.  We'll help you as much as we can.

00:15:10.780 --> 00:15:12.820
You must have been through a lot.

00:15:13.590 --> 00:15:14.430
Thank you.

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:16.210
I'm Sayuri.

00:15:16.210 --> 00:15:17.220
Please call me Mika.

00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:19.430
As for me, call me Chiko.

00:15:19.430 --> 00:15:20.680
Chiko-san?

00:15:20.680 --> 00:15:22.050
You got it.

00:15:39.480 --> 00:15:41.460
Hello, Mikamo-san.

00:15:42.780 --> 00:15:43.750
Hello.

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:46.850
I hate to interrupt this little gathering,

00:15:46.850 --> 00:15:48.630
but that seat's reserved for me.

00:15:50.370 --> 00:15:53.950
You'll have to forgive me.  I didn't see a seating number on it anywhere.

00:16:00.360 --> 00:16:02.390
Can you be more careful in the future?

00:16:02.390 --> 00:16:03.000
Sure.

00:16:06.620 --> 00:16:11.780
That's Koito Shunka-san.  She's the granddaughter of the founder of this school.

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:18.110
We put up with her but she's really scary.  There are rumors she goes out partying at night too.

00:16:24.710 --> 00:16:26.750
Is something wrong, Chiko-san?

00:16:27.400 --> 00:16:28.650
I'm fine.

00:16:51.780 --> 00:16:53.150
Guess it's my imagination.

00:17:08.330 --> 00:17:09.940
She tried to get me.

00:17:13.110 --> 00:17:17.340
But I shouldn't be having any more horrible experiences now.

00:17:18.020 --> 00:17:21.100
Things are different than they were with him.

00:17:24.120 --> 00:17:29.790
Is she really the one who will inherit Twenty Faces' spoils?

00:17:32.840 --> 00:17:35.630
I'm terribly sorry, young lady.

00:17:35.630 --> 00:17:38.390
If I had only gone to pick you up a little earlier...

00:17:38.880 --> 00:17:40.810
It's not your fault, Tome-san.

00:17:41.750 --> 00:17:45.560
How was school?  Did you make any friends?

00:17:45.560 --> 00:17:46.310
Yeah.

00:17:47.490 --> 00:17:50.020
Well, well.  That's great, isn't it?

00:17:59.720 --> 00:18:02.100
Good job spotting me.

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:04.370
I couldn't stop thinking about you.

00:18:04.910 --> 00:18:07.360
Were you waiting for me?

00:18:07.360 --> 00:18:10.180
Or maybe for Twenty Faces to reappear?

00:18:10.860 --> 00:18:15.630
You think that Twenty Faces is still alive, don't you?

00:18:16.120 --> 00:18:17.410
I don't know.

00:18:18.370 --> 00:18:23.200
That's why I've been watching, listening, and thinking for myself.

00:18:24.180 --> 00:18:26.720
He always said that to me.

00:18:26.720 --> 00:18:30.460
He said that's the quickest way to get to something.

00:18:31.140 --> 00:18:33.960
Will you search for him?  For Twenty Faces?

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:36.510
Yes.

00:18:37.700 --> 00:18:40.280
Then from this moment forth, you're a detective.

00:18:40.840 --> 00:18:43.530
Or you can say a seeker of truth.

00:18:43.530 --> 00:18:44.790
It's a dangerous life.

00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:49.290
Just standing still like I've been doing is much more frightening.

00:18:50.800 --> 00:18:55.000
Then I'll give this back to you to protect.

00:18:56.110 --> 00:18:58.630
The Anastasia Ruby?

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:01.970
Why do you have this?

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:08.250
I found it.  It was in a spot in the garden that you could easily see from your window.

00:19:10.160 --> 00:19:12.500
...until I restore it to you.

00:19:14.530 --> 00:19:16.860
It's possible that Twenty Faces is still alive.

00:19:20.600 --> 00:19:22.080
Let's have a race.

00:19:22.080 --> 00:19:26.510
Let's see which one of us can get to him first.

00:19:30.040 --> 00:19:31.030
Yes!

00:20:20.400 --> 00:20:22.220
Hey!  Hang in there!

00:20:22.850 --> 00:20:24.770
It's no good!  His neck's broken!

00:20:27.560 --> 00:20:28.860
A monster!
